EC–32. A letter from the Senior Congressional Liaison, Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, transmitting the Bureau’s advisory opinion rescinding previous advisory opinion — Truth in Lending (Regulation Z); Consumer Credit Offered to Borrowers in Advance of Expected Receipt of Compensation for Work [Docket No. CFPB–2024–0032] received January 8, 2025, pursuant to 5 U.S.C. 801(a)(1)(A); Public Law 104–121, Sec. 251; (110 Stat. 868); to the Committee on Financial Services. EC–33. A letter from the Chairman, National Credit Union Administration, transmitting the Administration’s Fair Hiring in Banking Act Report to Congress, pursuant to Public Law 117–263, Sec. 5705(c)(3); (136 Stat. 3411); to the Committee on Financial Services.

EC–34. A letter from the Biologist, U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service, Department of the Interior, transmitting the Department’s final rule — Endangered and Threatened Wildlife and Plants; Emergency Listing of the Blue Tree Monitor as an Endangered Species [Docket No. FWS–HQ–ES–2023–0033;

Natural Resources. EC–35. A letter from the Senior Congressional Liaison, Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, transmitting the Bureau’s Major final rule — Civil Penalty Inflation Adjustments received January 8, 2025, pursuant to 5 U.S.C. 801(a)(1)(A); Public Law 104121, Sec. 251; (110 Stat. 868); to the Committee on the Judiciary.
